WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.000
For some people, playing basketball helps them become leaders who work hard and get along with others.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.000
For others, basketball just feels like bouncing a wall and throwing it into a silly hoop.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
Same with negative events. For some, being exposed to parents fighting makes them feel afraid to go home.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
For others, it makes them angry and ready to fight.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.000
And for some kids, they ignore it and it doesn't really impact them at all.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:29.000
Think about when someone calls you names.

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Different kinds of name-calling might make you feel different ways.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:39.000
It probably matters what they say, who says it, how many times they say it, and who else hears it.

